0..79 Comment "/// A composite over a path typed at a stated lambda meets the composite at the"
80..100 Comment "/// lambda\'s reduct."
101..104 Comment "///"
105..183 Comment "/// `along`\'s type writes `F(x)`, so `along` at a stated lambda has the lambda"
184..254 Comment "/// applied at its endpoints. A composite over that path starts at the"
255..330 Comment "/// application. Passed to `composeHere`, whose type writes `p then q`, its"
331..407 Comment "/// start meets the reduct `F(x)` or the application written again. A lambda"
408..488 Comment "/// whose body composes, `fn (q) { q then g }`, meets a composite written apart."
489..492 Comment "///"
493..571 Comment "/// The conversion\'s code walk reads a call of a stated lambda as the lambda\'s"
572..651 Comment "/// body, its binder bound to the call\'s argument. Two composites written apart"
652..730 Comment "/// meet part by part. The kernel replays each declaration by its own reading."
731..734 Comment "///"
735..818 Comment "/// - see: #4073 — the checker refused a stated lambda applied against its reduct"
819..898 Comment "/// - see: #4065 — a call passed to a parameter, read as the value it returns"
899..951 Comment "/// - see: #3920 — one stated lambda written twice"
953..982 Comment "/// The action of `F` on `p`."
